Z||000016||DaRkLoRD||02-06-2001||03:44 PM||||most of the "conspiracy" stuff is just things covered up to protect the finances of the companies funding the government.. nothing too mysterious.<P>and I've personally seen 2 coverups. 1 of which got out, the other did not... (yet)<BR>There's a lot of stuff that the general public never hears about.. there could have been a fairly serious nuclear accident at a Canadian reactor station 2-3 years ago, but they never told the media. I worked at a nuclear plant for a year as part of a school co-op placement.. I find it scary that they didn't tell anyone what was happening.. governments do the same things, to protect their funding and to prevent public panic...<BR>which is why any/all alien encounters will be suppressed until the public is sufficiently "prepared" through the media.. for example, the idea of aliens is a lot more acceptable now than 30 years ago...<P>the one that got out was the water treatment stuff in Walkerton.. it got out because people started dying from the contamination.. but the problem was known about for YEARS before.. no one did anything, and records were falsified to make everything appear normal. This stuff happens in virtually every level of government.. sometimes it's easier to cover something up than deal with it.<P>------------------<BR>   <A HREF="mailto:steve@fieroproject.com">steve@fieroproject.com</A>   <BR><A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroproject.com</A><p>[This message has been edited by DaRkLoRD (edited 02-06-2001).]||||reg||4
